WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.340
Reports that Bam Margera was hospitalized in&nbsp;
December didn't explain just how close to death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.600
the "Jackass" star came. But now the daredevil&nbsp;
is giving the full story in his own words.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:15.240
To usher in the new millennium in grand fashion,&nbsp;
MTV debuted a show in October 2000 that remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.460
as culturally relevant and hilarious as ever:&nbsp;
"Jackass." If you're somehow unfamiliar with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:24.000
the series, it featured a group of stuntmen&nbsp;
and old friends doing pranks to each other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.600
and attempting wild stunts. To say it&nbsp;
became a hit would be an understatement

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.100
Some of the original stars of the show, including&nbsp;
Johnny Knoxville and Steve-O, have stayed in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.840
public eye and kept the legacy of "Jackass" alive.&nbsp;
But that hasn't been true for the entirety of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.280
original crew. For one, there's Bam Margera,&nbsp;
who has lived a roller coaster life since the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:46.140
now-iconic MTV series first gained prominence.&nbsp;
Margera has found himself in some terrifying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.460
and rather unsavory situations, including&nbsp;
drama with some of his "Jackass" co-stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.300
Knoxville among them. Nevertheless, he's&nbsp;
managed to power through and live to tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:58.920
his story all these years later. But Margera&nbsp;
revealed he recently came very close to death.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.060
On January 5, 2023, Margera&nbsp;
stopped by the "Steve-O's Wild&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.260
Ride!" podcast to commemorate the end of his&nbsp;
conservatorship. Before he could get to that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.140
though, he had a scary story from&nbsp;
the previous month to share with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:14.000
listeners. Right out of the gate, he&nbsp;
shared the news of his own "death."

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.820
"I basically was pronounced dead&nbsp;
on Elvis' birthday, December 8."

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.960
Margera didn't realize it, but he'd been&nbsp;
dealing with an extreme case of COVID-19.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.400
He added that his body started shutting down&nbsp;
and he had four seizures, each of which lasted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.200
between 10 and 20 minutes. The fourth was so&nbsp;
bad that he says he nearly bit off his tongue.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:35.880
Margera's tongue became swollen and began&nbsp;
bleeding. Margera then swallowed the blood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.500
which, in turn, resulted in him contracting&nbsp;
pneumonia. Worse yet, on his way to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.280
he went into a fifth seizure. With his&nbsp;
swollen tongue, he couldn't breathe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.880
When he finally came into the hospital, he&nbsp;
thought he'd only been there for a few hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.560
but he couldn't have been more wrong. Shortly&nbsp;
after waking up, he remembered being told,

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.980
"Like, 'Dude, you've been here for nearly&nbsp;
a week. We tried to take the tube out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.720
but you weren't breathing on your own."

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.240
Thankfully, eight days after&nbsp;
being admitted to the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:04.680
Margera made a full recovery and was&nbsp;
released. News outlets picked up on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.640
story almost immediately. Steve-O mentioned&nbsp;
that after hearing about it on the news and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.240
seeing Margera on a ventilator, he assumed&nbsp;
the worst was right around the corner.

00:02:12.385 --> 00:02:15.085
"I'm just thinking, 'Oh my God, this is it.'"

00:02:15.085 --> 00:02:18.780
While Margera was in the hospital, Steve-O&nbsp;
joked that if his friend didn't make it through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.680
that would throw a serious wrench&nbsp;
into his tour plans. Some fans loved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.960
the "Jackass"-style gallows humor; others didn't.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:30.480
Steve-O made sure to clarify that Margera's&nbsp;
recovery was the top priority. Margera chimed in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.160
with a laugh and compared his newly raspy voice,&nbsp;
thanks to the breathing tube, to that of Steve-O.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:39.000
Margera doesn't remember much of what happened&nbsp;
to him prior to waking up in the hospital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.200
saying that he essentially blacked out until&nbsp;
he opened his eyes in the hospital bed. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.380
safe to assume he didn't miss a whole&nbsp;
lot throughout his lengthy hospital stay.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.840
As if the past few years haven't shown it already,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.100
COVID-19 is no joke and is more than&nbsp;
capable of killing at a moment's notice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.180
It's good to hear that Bam Margera was&nbsp;
able to recover from the deadly disease.

